TODO BEFORE RELEASE

    * be explicit about the modulation type featured in the various
      clock modules - it probably does not work as people expect!

TODO NEW FEATURES FOR A FUTURE RELEASE (not next release)
    * allow user to specify relative note positions in riff_data
      by use of + symbol before position value.

    **DEBUG** the new EDITOR and UI_ITEM* workings. I seem to have fixed
      the earlier problem where it would always refuse to set an
      input from a multiple choice group within a specific instance of
      a module. My confidence isn't high that it's actually fixed yet,
      BECAUSE if you use -v on the commandline, on a file which
      previously had this problem, it completely suppresses the
      progress bar. A likely cause from internet search suggests a null
      string has likely been sent to std::cout and set it's error bit,
      which causes output suppression.

    * the whole header situation is a bit of a mess. I think the only
      place sample rate should be set within the file processed from
      the command line. Sample rate set in any included files will be
      verbosely ignored.

    * functionality to delete modules and rename modules

    * does autogrouping need 'autogroup_create' and 'autogroup_add'
      directives, not just the simpler 'autogroup'? - my thinking was
      to avoid confusion, force use of 'add' when the group already
      existed (for example in an included file) but might be missed.

    * investigate if param_editor and input_editor could be replaced
      with a single editor to handle both inputs and outputs

    * adsr_scaler - needs to be a bit more versatile - allow scaling of
      output levels as well as time, apply scale to upper, lower, not
      just both shapes.

    * wave_phase cycle sync can be a problem, using on_trig_reset_phase
      can cause clicks especially for regular waveforms, but even
      without, such as a sawtooth without on_trig_phase_reset, but with
      phase modulation, will have a single sample click every several
      cycles.

    * investigate possiblity for a parameter to specify the output
      type for those modules which process outputs from a list of other
      modules (switcher, trig_switcher, combiner, etc)

    * or better yet - investigate possibility of specifying outputs
      directily for those modules which currently process outputs from
      a list of modules (switcher, trig_switcher, combiner, etc).
      ie if the input_editor can do this... why can't that functionality
      be brought to modules that need it - and do away with the clunky
      adding of modules to modules!?
      -- tried adding optional output name parameter to dobjmod but
      combiner etc store each dobjmod as a linked list of
      synthmod::base* so no current way of storing which output to use.

    * rename data object (or directive?) for renaming stuff
      specifically groups, all the modules in the group, and their
      connections.

ideas

    * chain copy? set modules to copy as comma seperated list without
      whitespace (ie osc1,wave1,adsr1,amp1). set either name prefix, or
      name suffix, for renaming all copied modules. connections
      duplicated additionally.

    * creation loops with iterative values, basic maths, for creating
      copies of modules


